  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n2 4 8 0 0 0 0 0 0\n1 6 8 0 0 0 0 0 0\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n0 0 8 0 3 0 0 3 0\n0 0 8 3 3 3 3 3 3\n0 0 8 0 3 0 0 3 0\n0 0 8 0 3 0 0 3 0\n0 0 8 3 3 3 3 3 3\n0 0 8 0 3 0 0 3 0\nOutput:\n0 2 0 0 4 0\n2 2 2 4 4 4\n0 2 0 0 4 0\n0 1 0 0 6 0\n1 1 1 6 6 6\n0 1 0 0 6 0\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 0 0 0 8 1 2\n0 0 0 0 0 0 8 4 1\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n0 0 3 3 0 3 8 0 0\n3 3 0 0 0 0 8 0 0\n3 3 0 3 0 3 8 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 8 0 0\n3 3 3 3 3 3 8 0 0\n0 0 0 0 3 0 8 0 0\nOutput:\n0 0 1 2 0 2\n1 1 0 0 0 0\n1 1 0 2 0 2\n0 0 0 0 1 0\n4 4 4 1 1 1\n0 0 0 0 1 0\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n0 0 8 0 0 3 0 0 3\n0 0 8 0 0 3 0 0 3\n0 0 8 3 3 0 3 3 0\n0 0 8 0 0 0 0 3 0\n0 0 8 0 3 0 3 0 0\n0 0 8 0 3 0 0 0 3\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n2 4 8 0 0 0 0 0 0\n6 5 8 0 0 0 0 0 0\nOutput:\n0 0 2 0 0 4\n0 0 2 0 0 4\n2 2 0 4 4 0\n0 0 0 0 5 0\n0 6 0 5 0 0\n0 6 0 0 0 5\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 3 0 0 8 0 0\n3 3 0 3 0 3 8 0 0\n0 3 0 3 0 3 8 0 0\n0 3 3 3 0 0 8 0 0\n0 3 0 0 0 3 8 0 0\n0 0 3 0 0 0 8 0 0\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n0 0 0 0 0 0 8 2 1\n0 0 0 0 0 0 8 4 7\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    n = 9\n    # Locate the full row and column of 8s that form the cross\n    r8 = None\n    for i in range(n):\n        if all(grid[i][j] == 8 for j in range(n)):\n            r8 = i\n            break\n    c8 = None\n    for j in range(n):\n        if all(grid[i][j] == 8 for i in range(n)):\n            c8 = j\n            break\n\n    # Determine the 2x2 key quadrant and the opposite 6x6 mask quadrant\n    if r8 == 2 and c8 == 2:          # key top-left\n        key_rows = range(0, 2)\n        key_cols = range(0, 2)\n        mask_rows = range(3, 9)\n        mask_cols = range(3, 9)\n    elif r8 == 2 and c8 == 6:        # key top-right\n        key_rows = range(0, 2)\n        key_cols = range(7, 9)\n        mask_rows = range(3, 9)\n        mask_cols = range(0, 6)\n    elif r8 == 6 and c8 == 2:        # key bottom-left\n        key_rows = range(7, 9)\n        key_cols = range(0, 2)\n        mask_rows = range(0, 6)\n        mask_cols = range(3, 9)\n    else:                             # key bottom-right (r8==6 and c8==6)\n        key_rows = range(7, 9)\n        key_cols = range(7, 9)\n        mask_rows = range(0, 6)\n        mask_cols = range(0, 6)\n\n    # Extract the 2x2 key and the 6x6 mask\n    key = [[grid[i][j] for j in key_cols] for i in key_rows]\n    mask = [[grid[i][j] for j in mask_cols] for i in mask_rows]\n\n    # Build the 6x6 output by filling the four 3x3 mask blocks\n    out = [[0] * 6 for _ in range(6)]\n    for br in range(2):\n        for bc in range(2):\n            val = key[br][bc]\n            base_r = br * 3\n            base_c = bc * 3\n            for i in range(3):\n                for j in range(3):\n                    if mask[base_r + i][base_c + j] != 0:\n                        out[base_r + i][base_c + j] = val\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    n = 9\n    # Locate the full row and column of 8s that form the cross\n    r8 = None\n    for i in range(n):\n        if all(grid[i][j] == 8 for j in range(n)):\n            r8 = i\n            break\n    c8 = None\n    for j in range(n):\n        if all(grid[i][j] == 8 for i in range(n)):\n            c8 = j\n            break\n\n    # Determine the 2x2 key quadrant and the opposite 6x6 mask quadrant\n    if r8 == 2 and c8 == 2:          # key top-left\n        key_rows = range(0, 2)\n        key_cols = range(0, 2)\n        mask_rows = range(3, 9)\n        mask_cols = range(3, 9)\n    elif r8 == 2 and c8 == 6:        # key top-right\n        key_rows = range(0, 2)\n        key_cols = range(7, 9)\n        mask_rows = range(3, 9)\n        mask_cols = range(0, 6)\n    elif r8 == 6 and c8 == 2:        # key bottom-left\n        key_rows = range(7, 9)\n        key_cols = range(0, 2)\n        mask_rows = range(0, 6)\n        mask_cols = range(3, 9)\n    else:                             # key bottom-right (r8==6 and c8==6)\n        key_rows = range(7, 9)\n        key_cols = range(7, 9)\n        mask_rows = range(0, 6)\n        mask_cols = range(0, 6)\n\n    # Extract the 2x2 key and the 6x6 mask\n    key = [[grid[i][j] for j in key_cols] for i in key_rows]\n    mask = [[grid[i][j] for j in mask_cols] for i in mask_rows]\n\n    # Build the 6x6 output by filling the four 3x3 mask blocks\n    out = [[0] * 6 for _ in range(6)]\n    for br in range(2):\n        for bc in range(2):\n            val = key[br][bc]\n            base_r = br * 3\n            base_c = bc * 3\n            for i in range(3):\n                for j in range(3):\n                    if mask[base_r + i][base_c + j] != 0:\n                        out[base_r + i][base_c + j] = val\n    return out",
